  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 108 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nTuesday through Friday:\n\nNorthwest flow at 500 mb is generally expected to remain over\nthe region through the rest of next week, with the ridge axis\nperhaps slowly shifting east and flattening out. It appears from\nensembles that high pressure should build into the region for\nTuesday into Wednesday, bringing warm and humid conditions but\nkeeping dew points and heat index values lower than Sunday and \nMonday. More active weather may return to the area later this\nweek, as low pressure and a cold front tries to shift southeast\nthrough the region. The warm and humid conditions should linger\nas well, per ensemble member trends and continued small NBM\ntemperature spreads.\n\nWood",
